    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48863" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trans-pădānus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that is beyond the Po</i>, <i>Transpadane</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 17, 21, § 123</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Italia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 29, 41, § 77</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coloni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 3, 87</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clientes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 12, 5, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alarii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 17, 7</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Transpădāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the nations beyond the Po</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 18,
				13, 34, § 127</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 5, 2
					<i>fin.</i></span></i>; Cael. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 8,
				1, 2</span></i>.—<i>Sing.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Transpadanus,</span>”
				<i>a man from beyond the Po</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					39, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
